Now I have everything I need to produce a thorough, concrete plan. Let me compose it.

---

## Implementation Plan: Web UI Build for ComfyUI Agent Sidebar

### Analysis of Existing State

**What exists and works:**
- `sidebar.js`: AgentConnection class with reconnect logic is solid. The `sendMessage()` + workflow capture pattern is correct. The message handler switch on `data.type` is the right shape. Keep all of it, extend it.
- `routes.py`: Emits `text_delta`, `stage`, `message`, `error`, `done`. The `_run_agent_sync` / `_forward_event` pipeline is the right seam for panel injection. The `on_tool_call` callback fires synchronously with the tool name and input, but crucially it fires before the tool result is available. Panel emission needs to happen after the result returns, not when the call is dispatched.
- `summarize_workflow_data()`: Returns a rich dict with `format`, `node_count`, `connection_count`, `editable_field_count`, `summary`, `nodes`, `editable_fields`. This is the primary source for workflow analysis panels.

**The key architectural insight for panel emission:**

`run_agent_turn` in `main.py` calls `on_tool_call(tc.name, tc.input)` BEFORE executing the tool, then stores the result in `tool_results`. The result is a JSON string. Currently `routes.py` only hooks `on_tool_call` for stage inference, not for the result. To emit panels, `routes.py` needs to intercept results — either by wrapping `handle_tool` or by adding an `on_tool_result` callback to `run_agent_turn`. The latter is cleaner and consistent with the existing callback pattern.

---

## Phase 1: CSS + Typography + Chat UI Restyle

**Goal:** Everything looks right, text renders with proper typography. No panels yet. Completely demoable.

### `ui/web/css/superduper.css` — Complete rewrite

The file needs to be rebuilt around CSS custom properties (design tokens), then all components defined against those tokens. Structure:

**Section 1 — Design tokens (`:root`)**

```css
:root {
  /* Brand */
  --sd-brand:         #00BB81;
  --sd-brand-dim:     #00BB8133;
  --sd-brand-subtle:  #00BB8118;

  /* Surfaces */
  --sd-canvas:        #0d0f14;
  --sd-panel:         #141620;
  --sd-card:          #1a1d2a;
  --sd-card-hover:    #1e2133;
  --sd-elevated:      #222538;
  --sd-input-bg:      #12141e;

  /* Text */
  --sd-text-primary:   #e8e9ed;
  --sd-text-secondary: #9a9caa;
  --sd-text-muted:     #5c5e6e;
  --sd-text-accent:    #c0c2ce;

  /* Borders */
  --sd-border-subtle:  #1f2230;
  --sd-border-mid:     #2a2d40;

  /* Slot colors */
  --sd-slot-clip:       #FFD500;
  --sd-slot-clip-v:     #A8DADC;
  --sd-slot-cond:       #FFA931;
  --sd-slot-ctrl:       #6EE7B7;
  --sd-slot-image:      #64B5F6;
  --sd-slot-latent:     #FF9CF9;
  --sd-slot-mask:       #81C784;
  --sd-slot-model:      #B39DDB;
  --sd-slot-style:      #C2FFAE;
  --sd-slot-vae:        #FF6E6E;
  --sd-slot-noise:      #B0B0B0;
  --sd-slot-guider:     #66FFFF;
  --sd-slot-sampler:    #ECB4B4;
  --sd-slot-sigmas:     #CDFFCD;

  /* Typography */
  --sd-font-sans: "Inter", "SF Pro Display", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --sd-font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", "SF Mono", monospace;

  /* Spacing */
  --sd-space-xs:   4px;
  --sd-space-sm:   6px;
  --sd-space-md:   10px;
  --sd-space-lg:   14px;
  --sd-space-xl:   16px;

  /* Transitions */
  --sd-transition: 150ms ease;
}
```

**Section 2 — Font injection**

The `sidebar.js` already injects its own CSS link. The Google Fonts link should be injected similarly, or better: placed at the very top of the CSS file as an `@import` rule. Since ComfyUI serves this file directly, `@import url(...)` for Google Fonts works fine.

```css
@import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;600&display=swap");
```

**Section 3 — Layout shell** (panel, header, messages area, input bar)

Everything previously using `#4a9eff` switches to `var(--sd-brand)`. The stage bar background changes from `#1a2a3a` to `var(--sd-card)`. All hardcoded hex colors become token references.

Key changes from current CSS:
- `.sd-header__title` color: `#4a9eff` -> `var(--sd-brand)`, font-family adds `var(--sd-font-sans)`
- `.sd-stage__label` color: `#4a9eff` -> `var(--sd-brand)`
- `.sd-send-btn` background: `#4a9eff` -> `var(--sd-brand)`, text: `#fff` -> `#020410` (dark on brand green reads better than white)
- `.sd-input:focus` border-color: `#4a9eff` -> `var(--sd-brand)`
- `.sd-message--user` background: `#2a3a4a` -> `var(--sd-card)` with a brand-dim left border
- `.sd-message--agent` background: `#333` -> `var(--sd-panel)`
- All message body text gets `font-family: var(--sd-font-sans)`

**Section 4 — Text rendering classes** (new, no equivalent in current CSS)

These classes are applied by the text renderer in chat.js:

```css
/* Text message body — applied by createTextBody() */
.sd-text-body {
  font-family: var(--sd-font-sans);
  font-size: 12px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--sd-text-secondary);
}

.sd-text-body p {
  margin: 0 0 8px 0;
}
.sd-text-body p:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* Inline code (backtick spans) */
.sd-code-inline {
  font-family: var(--sd-font-mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  background: var(--sd-elevated);
  padding: 1px 5px;
  border-radius: 3px;
  color: var(--sd-text-accent);
}

/* Code blocks (triple backtick) */
.sd-code-block {
  font-family: var(--sd-font-mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  background: var(--sd-input-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--sd-border-subtle);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  margin: 8px 0;
  overflow-x: auto;
  color: var(--sd-text-accent);
  white-space: pre;
}

/* Bold spans */
.sd-text-bold {
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--sd-text-primary);
}
```

**Section 5 — Panel components** (needed for Phase 2 but define the CSS now)

The 7 design system components as CSS rules. These are dead rules in Phase 1 but allow Phase 2 to drop in DOM without any CSS changes:

```css
/* Panel wrapper */
.sd-panel { ... }
.sd-panel-header { ... }
.sd-panel-header__label { font-family: var(--sd-font-mono); font-size: 10px; ... }
.sd-panel-header__badge { ... }
.sd-panel-header__title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; ... }
.sd-panel-header__summary { ... }
.sd-panel-header__stats { ... }
.sd-stat-number { font-family: var(--sd-font-mono); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
.sd-stat-label { font-size: 10px; }

/* Collapsible section */
.sd-section { ... }
.sd-section__trigger { ... }
.sd-section__trigger--open .sd-section__chevron { transform: rotate(90deg); }
.sd-section__chevron { transition: transform var(--sd-transition); }
.sd-section__body { ... }
.sd-section__body--collapsed { display: none; }

/* Slot tag */
.sd-slot-tag { font-family: var(--sd-font-mono); font-size: 11px; ... }
.sd-slot-tag__dot { width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; }

/* Flow chain */
.sd-flow-chain { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 4px; }
.sd-flow-node { font-family: var(--sd-font-mono); font-size: 11px; ... }
.sd-flow-arrow { color: var(--sd-text-muted); font-size: 12px; }

